From 22ef494bdaf6cd022f5c2021941dff0fe5553d9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:23:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Subtitles] Judge a bitmap subtitle as text or graphic once
 per stream

A Blu-ray may compose its subtitles into one large PGS bitmap together
with other artwork rather than emitting a small image per line. Measured
on a 3D subtitle demo disc: one bitmap of 1177x1026 at (130,40) in a
1920x1080 frame, carrying an on-screen label near the top and the
subtitle line near the bottom, and re-emitted as it grows - 169x114
while only the label is up.

Scaling such a bitmap about its centre moves the text inside it. The
bitmap centre is at x=718.5 while the subtitle line is centred at
x=946.5, so the line shifted by (zoom - 1) * 228 px: measured +114 px at
150%, and left at 60%. The content inset cannot help, as the content
genuinely fills the bitmap.

RepositionBitmapSubtitles already declined to move an overlay taller
than a third of the picture. Judging each bitmap on its own flips that
decision as the disc re-emits a growing one, so the label changed size
and jumped its line whenever the subtitle came and went. The tallest
content seen in the current subtitle stream now decides, for the zoom
and for the repositioning alike, which cannot oscillate.
CVideoPlayerSubtitle numbers each opening of a subtitle stream and
stamps its overlays with it, so switching track, embedded or external,
starts afresh, while a seek stays within the stream and keeps the
verdict. The height is kept as a share of the whole video picture, not
of the part left on screen, so neither a change of view size nor video
zoom reclassifies it.

A disc that emits one bitmap per line is unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

[Hades: NoteBitmapContentHeight() and IsLineOfText() placed by hand right before
GetContentRect(), which in this tree follows SubtitleDepth() (Blu-ray 3D depth). Same lines
added and removed as the origin, 71beb886f226.]
